                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq x
          %p
            Typically the notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⌊
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⌋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lfloor{x}\rfloor
            is used when both floor and ceiling appear, but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
